WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.540
Eighteenth-century Königsberg.

2
00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:06.070
A river runs through the
town, around two islands.

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.700
Two banks, two islands:
four pieces of land,

4
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.790
joined by seven bridges.

5
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.100
The townspeople tried a challenge.

6
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.830
Walk a route that crosses
each bridge exactly once.

7
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.320
Not one bridge missed,
not one crossed twice.

8
00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.140
Does such a walk exist?

9
00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:26.380
Does it depend on where you
start, or where you finish?

10
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.700
In this mission, you'll
redraw the map as a graph:

11
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.410
each piece of land a
vertex, each bridge an edge.

12
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.270
You'll meet the degree of a vertex,
the number of edges meeting it.

13
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.740
And a trail, a walk that
never repeats an edge.

14
00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:45.870
Your mission: decide whether you can
cross all seven bridges exactly once.
